Subject: [PATCH] A function that tail-jumps to its own address has not returned (TODO 357)

PS2Runtime::afterCall takes "the callee left pc at its own entry" for "it did not set pc (a stub): it has returned"
and puts the caller's return address in. A jump through a pointer can target the jumping function itself: a
decorator that forwards a virtual to its child's same slot by `jr $t9`, when the child shares the function
(slChainedPositionBehaviour::vfunc_02 on a spread behaviour over a sphere behaviour; flStreamDecorator's
forwarders on nested decorators; 28 functions of the game have this shape). The jump was dropped and the child
never got the call - unless a checkpoint happened to be due at the jump, when the old way through the dispatcher
entered it.

dispatchGuestBranch now remembers a jump's target and the call level it was made at (two thread-local words, in
ps2_runtime.cpp only: no header changes), and afterCall applies its rule only when the callee did not just jump
to its own entry at that level. The callee is then entered again by afterCall's own continuation (the same
checkpoints as for any other address a call went on at), or by the dispatcher where that is off. A stub that
left pc alone records nothing and is "returned" as before. Nothing new can spin: one more entry per jump, each
behind a checkpoint; 2^20 such jumps in one go are logged once and left to the dispatcher, as any guest loop.

The jump record is read once and cleared on every way out of a call's end (a stop, a thread's end, the
continuation, a thread switch's unwind): it is not carried past the call it was made in.

PS2X_SELF_JUMP=0: the old rule (A/B). PS2X_SELF_JUMP_LOG=1: `[runtime] self jump: <function> ...` lines at the
1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th ... jump of each function, with either rule.

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
index 3411b3d..7ea8961 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_runtime.cpp
@@ -2025,6 +2025,34 @@ namespace
     const bool g_plainSwitches = !g_ps2HotStats && !envOff("PS2X_DISPATCH_LEAN") && !envOn("PS2X_DISPATCH_HISTORY");
     const bool g_plainCalls = g_plainSwitches && !envOff("PS2X_LEAN_CALL") && !envOff("PS2X_DIRECT_CALLS");
     const bool g_plainBranchCalls = g_plainSwitches && !envOff("PS2X_LEAN_BRANCH");
+
+    // (0195, TODO 357) A function that tail-jumps to its OWN address is not a function that returned.
+    // afterCall takes "the callee left pc at its own entry" for "it did not set pc: a stub, it has returned" and puts
+    // the caller's return address in. But a jump through a pointer can target the jumping function itself: a
+    // decorator forwarding a virtual to its child's same slot (`lw $a0, child; lw $t9, vtable; lw $t9, slot($t9);
+    // jr $t9`) whose child shares the function - slChainedPositionBehaviour::vfunc_02 on a spread behaviour over a
+    // sphere behaviour, flStreamDecorator's forwarders on nested decorators. The jump was dropped: the child never
+    // got the call. dispatchGuestBranch now remembers a jump's target and the call level it was made at; afterCall
+    // applies its rule only when the callee did not just jump there. A stub that merely left pc alone records
+    // nothing, so it is "returned" as before; nothing loops here that did not before - the callee is entered once
+    // more by the code below (its usual checkpoints), and a function that jumps to itself without end is a guest
+    // loop the dispatcher runs as it runs any other (kSelfJumpGuard jumps in one go: logged once, then left to it).
+    // PS2X_SELF_JUMP=0: the old rule (A/B). PS2X_SELF_JUMP_LOG=1: each such jump counted by function, a line at
+    // 1, 2, 4, 8 ... (`[runtime] self jump`), honoured or cut short.
+    thread_local uint32_t t_jumpTarget = 0u, t_jumpLevel = 0u;
+    const bool g_selfJump = !envOff("PS2X_SELF_JUMP");
+    const bool g_selfJumpLog = envOn("PS2X_SELF_JUMP_LOG");
+    constexpr uint32_t kSelfJumpGuard = 1u << 20;
+    void noteSelfJump(uint32_t entry, uint32_t returnsTo, bool honoured)
+    {
+        static std::mutex mutex;
+        static std::unordered_map<uint32_t, uint64_t> counts;
+        std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+        const uint64_t n = ++counts[entry];
+        if ((n & (n - 1u)) == 0u)
+            std::fprintf(stderr, "[runtime] self jump: %08x jumps to its own entry (its caller goes on at %08x): %llu so far, %s\n", entry,
+                         returnsTo, static_cast<unsigned long long>(n), honoured ? "entered again" : "cut short (PS2X_SELF_JUMP=0)");
+    }
 }
 
